  "adaptedRules": [
    "All first forms with three-stage chains in the current snapshot join the previous starters. Dratini learns Ember at level 7 as a game-only exception. A fighter with no learned damaging moves may use Struggle even while status PP remain.",
    "Release removes only the selected partner and returns its held item. Currency, inventory, day and fatigue persist; releasing the last partner makes a new egg available.",
    "Sinnoh evolution locations and game day/night are selectable contexts. NPC trade consumes a 150-point trade pass and, when required, a separately purchased 300-point evolution item. Tyrogue attack/defense IVs persist; other IVs are zero and EVs/natures are not modeled.",
    "Wild opponents: 146 Kanto species excluding Articuno, Zapdos, Moltres, Mewtwo and Mew. Kanto-only evolution stages; middle gates >=20; final gates >=36 and actual minimum evolution level; non-evolving species >=20 or >=30 for base stat total >=450. Enemy level is partner level minus 0 to 2.",
    "Game day advances by sleeping, not real-world date.",
    "Daily fatigue 100; battle +35; feeding +15; sleep resets.",
    "One starter hatches at level 7: Dratini, Eevee and Ditto each 2%; 39 other starters share 94% equally. Pichu replaces Pikachu for new eggs. Up to three partners including captures; shared fatigue. Feed friendship +12, sleep +3, level-up +5.",
    "Battle win rewards active partner XP = floor(0.8 × (40 + 3 × enemy level squared)) and 80 points. Evolution stones must first be bought in the shop for 300 points each.",
    "One-on-one battle simplifies utility, weather, trapping and some secondary effects. No abilities, EVs/natures or breeding. Held items listed in data/items.json are supported, including Gen IX Clear Amulet and Covert Cloak within modeled effects. Active partner fainting ends battle.",
    "PP is restored each encounter; learning slots remain capped at four.",
    "Move Reminder is free for the current species level-up learnset at or below current level.",
    "Shiny chance is 0.04 per egg or wild encounter, independently rolled. Existing Pokemon are not rerolled.",
    "HGSS catch probability uses HP, species capture rate, ball and status modifiers with integer rounding, then multiplies final success probability by 1.1 capped at 1.",
    "Battle medicines, failed capture attempts and switching consume a turn. Potions restore 20 HP; Super Potions restore 50 HP. Status conditions end with battle.",
    "Added all 14 three-stage roots introduced in Generation III and their Generation III evolutions (44 species), plus Pichu. HGSS learnsets and Gen IV stats/types are used. Wurmple branch is independently assigned once at creation, 50% Silcoon / 50% Cascoon, preserved in saves. Ralts follows Gardevoir; Gallade is outside this Generation III addition."
  ],
